<section class="help-card help-card--compact">
  {% if building.editorial_representative %}
    <div class="help-card__eyebrow">District context</div>
    <h2 class="help-card__title">How to read this building</h2>
  {% else %}
    <div class="help-card__eyebrow">Before you lease</div>
    <h2 class="help-card__title">What to evaluate about this space</h2>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="help-card__grid help-card__grid--tight">
    <div class="help-card__item">
      <h3>{% if building.editorial_representative %}District role{% else %}Layout fit{% endif %}</h3>
      <p>
        {% if building.editorial_representative %}
          Use the building as a reference point for the district's commercial form, not as a statement about current availability.
        {% else %}
          Make sure the layout supports your workflow, staffing, or customer experience.
        {% endif %}
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="help-card__item">
      <h3>{% if building.editorial_representative %}Street context{% else %}Total cost{% endif %}</h3>
      <p>
        {% if building.editorial_representative %}
          Compare the surrounding blocks, transit access, nearby services, and relationship to adjacent districts.
        {% else %}
          Ask about operating expenses, deposits, improvements, and utilities—not just rent.
        {% endif %}
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="help-card__item">
      <h3>{% if building.editorial_representative %}Commercial fit{% else %}Access and visibility{% endif %}</h3>
      <p>
        {% if building.editorial_representative %}
          Read the role label as commercial geography guidance, not as a complete inventory or ranking.
        {% else %}
          Consider parking, foot traffic, loading access, and how easy the space is to reach.
        {% endif %}
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
